
                           !!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!
                           ! REALLY IMPORTANT! !
                           !!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!

This  is  supposd  to  be  the final release of TransAmiga.  There are many
features  I  wanted to incorporate in TA, but I couldn't due to limitations
of the compiler.

I  planed to release the successor of TransAmiga in the middle of 1999, but
I  did  not have the luck to keep my time table so this maintenance release
of  TA  became  necessary.   The  new BBS progam which will be published as
TransComm  BBS  is  written  in  C++.   Unfortunately  I have to fight with
compiler  bugs  all  the  time.   Those  of you who have some experience in
programming  will agree that this can be a major obstacle especially if the
updatee of the compiler is not released for an extensive time.  Currently I
am  changing  to  GNU C.  I need some time to get to know that compiler and
find  all  those  little  differnces.  TransComm won't be shareware.  Noone
will have to pay anything to use it.

Right  now  I  am working on my diploma theses so there is not enough spare
time  to  do  all I want to.  I will finish my studies in February 2000 and
the  job  I  have been offered leaves me enough spare time to get some work
done.

In  the  age of the Internet there has to be a bunch of features to get the
BBS  some  attractive  features.  I did a lot of research and hope that the
final result is interesting for some of you.

---------------------------------------------------------------------------

The  GUI  version  of  TransCfg, the config program, is included in the bin
directory.

---------------------------------------------------------------------------


                                ATTENTION!

AsXPR  does NOT handle resumes correctly! I suggest you don't use it unless
you  don't  allow  ZModem  resume or similar protocols. AsXPR allows resume
protocols  to function, but it does not tell the BBS that it got a file. So
you  end  up  with an upload that is stored in the directory but not in the
file  description (Files.BBS). For those who don't know AsXPR: you have not
to worry about it.

There  was  no  time  to  update the German docs so I did not include them.

As  usual  the  update/install  archive of TA is uploaded to Aminet and all
support boards.

